# Copy to .env.local and restart `npm run dev` after editing.

# --- TURN relay (needed for collaborative shots on strict networks) ---------
#
# Two browsers connect directly when at least one side's NAT is permissive.
# Mobile carriers, CGNAT-ing ISPs and corporate wifi usually are not, and then
# the connection fails with "your two networks will not allow a direct link".
# A TURN server relays the (still end-to-end encrypted) packets as a fallback.
#
# There is no longer a working credential-free public TURN server. Free tiers
# that do work, pick one and paste its credentials below:
#   - https://dashboard.metered.ca/     (free tier, per-app credentials)
#   - https://www.expressturn.com/      (free tier)
#   - Cloudflare Realtime TURN          (free allotment)
#
# Comma-separated. Include the TLS/TCP 443 entry — it is the one that gets
# through networks that block UDP.
# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:global.relay.metered.ca:80,turn:global.relay.metered.ca:443,turns:global.relay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=your-turn-username
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-turn-credential

# --- Signaling -------------------------------------------------------------
# Only set this if the signaling server is NOT reachable at /rtc on the same
# origin as the app (the dev proxy and a normal reverse proxy both handle that).
# VITE_SIGNAL_URL=wss://your-server.example.com/rtc
